@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-preserve-json-merge-patch-immutability
+type: decision-log
+title: "Preserve JSON Merge Patch immutability"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` already returns a new JSON document and rejects non-JSON values. JSON Merge Patch must
+provide the same safe library boundary while following RFC 7386's recursive object semantics.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate and clone both `target` and `patch` before merging. Reuse the module's JSON validation and
+safe member-definition helpers; merge only JSON objects recursively, with arrays and scalar values
+replacing their targets.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers can retain and reuse either input after applying a patch. Invalid JSON values, cyclic inputs,
+and unsafe object shapes are rejected consistently with `applyPatch`.
